title: Campaigning
new-page: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
max-visits: 36
is-card: true
card-image: img/media_1.png
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

[? if npp_party_chair == "Remma" : Make friends. Be natural. <span class="tooltip-new">You've<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> always advocated for low profile but consistent campaigns. <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> interrupts your train of thought as he shows us another opportunity to spread our word. You tell him that you feel egotistic just heading this. He asks if you think you’re not ready for it. The air rushes out of your lungs. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Clueless" : Same old schedules. Same old strategies. There’s eventually a point where <span class="tooltip-new">you're<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Clueless.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ clueless_description +]</span></span> tired of it all. Again and again your calendar is dotted out with the same schedules. You still feel that passion inside of you, but it's exhausting to show up to these things in the first place. Nobody gets shit done fast enough without you sometimes. As you lay down in your bed staring at the ceiling, <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> interrupt. Another event we can hold. “Where can we go?” ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Ka San" : Your ass hurts as the ride back to HQ is with a rapidly moving jeepney. <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Clueless<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Clueless.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ clueless_description +]</span></span> are beside <span class="tooltip-new">you<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/KaSan.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ kasan_description +]</span></span> as they discuss more events to hold. The revolutionary and violent future you’ve always hoped for shouldn't probably look like this. You should be thinking about shooting <span class="tooltip-new">Yuuto<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Yuuto.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ yuuto_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Blooky<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Blooky.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ blooky_description +]</span></span> in the head. As the ride continues on your way home from the rally, your busmates talk about another one. “Santi, where do we go next?” ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Robbie" : A picture of <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span>, our former <span class="tooltip-new">Chancellor<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Chancellor.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ chancellor_description +]</span></span>, the old cabinet, and <span class="tooltip-new">you<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Robbie.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ barnabus_description +]</span></span> sits on the desk. You’re alone for a while before the former shows up. We’re gonna do the usual anyway, put up some posters, edit some paragraphs, then publish them all in the hopes of better poll numbers. Usually, you have fun doing these types of things. There’s something different today. You ask Remma if this planning session would be happier if we had them by our side. He doesn't answer, but he’s shaken to the core. You weep. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Macalintal" : Get the ball rolling. That’s what <span class="tooltip-new">you've<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span>, always been saying, as long as we start early we’ll be able to jump up our results. <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span>, interrupts your musings as he talks about how there's a free opportunity to hold a campaign, those meet-and-greets whatever. You tell him that you’ve never felt like it was right for you to be the one going out for this. He replies that you’re the chairperson anyway. He trusts you to make decisions. Do you? ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" : Ever since you’ve come into the scene, you’ve always pushed for the NPP to gather more casually and closely. No more of those LARP agreements whatever, you gotta act tough for the cameras. This time, you’re in a bar as <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Santi<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/KaSan.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ kasan_description +]</span></span> talk to you about our next event. Before you order another round, Santi asks you if you’ll slip up and say that word again before she laughs. Remma ignores her at the side, and tells you that he’ll be with you at your next destination. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Nakayama" : You’ve always hated showing yourself off to others. At least that’s what you’ve convinced yourself to believe. As you sit with <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> discussing your next places to campaign, you just wish for a place where you can be yourself and be accepted. <span class="tooltip-new">Naomi<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Naomi.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ naomi_description +]</span></span> hate it when you feel like you’re only taken seriously with a mask on. Remma snaps you out of your thinking, and asks if you’re willing to go to one more event. You ask him if they’ll like you. He doesn’t tell you anything that you could have told yourself. He asks you to believe, to have faith. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Danni" : What to do. What to do. <span class="tooltip-new">You<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Paisco.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ paisco_description +]</span></span> were never sure when you took up this position in the first place. The only thing you can think about is if you’ll do something wrong. You're scared of messing up, of doing nothing. <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> assures you that you’re a good person, but what does it mean when you can’t do anything at all? The list of potential places Remma shows you looks like a word search, you can’t decipher any of these terms. But you have the energy to at least try. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Ka Fil" : All these exercises, all these events, it’s all <span class="tooltip-new">your<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/KaFil.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ kafil_description +]</span></span> calling. You’re the expert in getting people riled up. You’re the expert in making things look funny, appealing, and strong. <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> come over for the usual, asking you to do these things for the party. Is that all you’re good for??]

- @workers
- @new_middle
- @old_middle
- @rural
- @unemployed
- @davao_campaign
- @discard_campaign
- @return_campaign

@workers
title: [? if npp_party_chair == "Clueless" or npp_party_chair == "Macalintal" or npp_party_chair == "Remma" : We can always try with the urban working class, they're our people. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Ka San" or npp_party_chair == "Ka Fil" : I’ve done this a hundred times before, let’s get back into the unions. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Robbie" : You know, they always loved talking about unionizing, let’s visit our workers. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" : Lets move to the docks, the factories, and the trade unions. Remind them who’s boss. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Nakayama" : Alright, let’s try something new. I’ve never been around workers before but we can manage with our new merging. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Paisco" : Uhh the urban workers, maybe I can try connecting with these humble people. ?]
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!

Q.resources -= 1; 

if (Q.unemployment >= 15) {
    Q.workers_npp -= 2;
}
if (Q.unemployment >= 25) {
    Q.workers_npp -= 2;
}
if (Q.nationalization_progress >= 1) {
    Q.workers_npp += 3*(1-dissent);
}

if (Q.npp_party_chair == "Shooter" || Q.npp_party_chair == "Ka San") {
    Q.workers_npp += 3*(1-dissent);
}

!}

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/workers_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">
[? if unemployed < 15 and npp_party_chair != "Shooter" and npp_party_chair != "Santi": The proletariat likes people who aren’t sentimental, who are men of action. You shake their hands, feeling their calluses, a few rallies bring up images of hope. Their stares convert into heavy weights placed on your shoulders. If you fail them, you’ve damned a thousand souls into thinking there’s a way out. ?]
[? if unemployed >= 15 and npp_party_chair != "Shooter" and npp_party_chair != "Santi": You try going house to house, convincing people of your cause. But they just want to hear about the economy. On how you’ve failed. If only they trusted you to talk about something else ?]
[? if npp_party_chair = "Shooter" or npp_party_chair = "Santi": Their anger is something raw, something terrifying. While your rallies are filled with chants of revolution and breaking the backs of the elite, you have to remind yourself that others can harness this emotion too. ?]
</div></div>

@new_middle
title: [? if npp_party_chair == "Clueless" or npp_party_chair == "Macalintal" or npp_party_chair == "Remma" : Why can't we work with the intelligentsia? We came from there, we can negotiate. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Ka San" or npp_party_chair == "Ka Fil" : I know how to talk to these elitistas, let’s send them an olive branch, we gotta build up our revolutionary potential. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Robbie" : We met in school, remember? These students are just like us, let’s give them and their parents a visit. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" : I hate these educated elites with a passion, but c’mon there’s gotta be something we have to give them. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Nakayama" : Yes. My people. College students. I’ll be accepted this time. Surely. Let’s visit their families too.  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Paisco" : The local government offices on the list look nice, why don’t we give them a visit? ?]
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!

Q.resources -= 1; 

Q.new_middle_npp += 6*(1-dissent); 
Q.resources -= 1;

if (Q.socialism <= 49) {
    Q.new_middle_npp -= 4;
}

!}

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/fun_students_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">
[? if socialism <= 49 : The first question received in your summit is about if our policies will remove personal delivery drivers. What a joke. These students, professors, and civil servants that gathered here will think of themselves first. They’ll fuck off to the nearest country if it means getting a single dime more, and they’ll forget about the ones left behind here. The poor, the ones who need their help the most. You feel your head ache as you realise these people are no more than performative, but we’ll be able to change that. We just have to make them comfortable with the idea of fighting for the greater good. More prodding is needed.  ?] 
[? if socialism > 49: You pose for the cameras as you shake hands with left-wing student organizations, NGOs, and civil servant unions They are star-struck by your “revolutionary” fervor and position, seemingly advising you on your next moves. You have no problems talking about and affirming their want for radical change, but their idealism impales a stake at your heart. If only you could kill them all. If only it were that easy.  ?]
</div></div>

@old_middle
title: [? if npp_party_chair == "Clueless" or npp_party_chair == "Macalintal" or npp_party_chair == "Remma" : The middle class, despite its elitist roots, cannot be ignored. I'll have to harden my heart and ring up some landlords. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Ka San" or npp_party_chair == "Ka Fil" : Evil, devil spawn. Some of the younger ones are redeemable, let’s shave them off so we have potential allies for a united front.  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Robbie" : Businesses are my people. Do you remember when we all gathered at my house? We haven’t even finished the dinosaur rock you gave us. I wish we all came again. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" : You told me about these open-minded small businesses we can talk to? Maybe I’ll try marketing socialism to them. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Nakayama" : Businesses. I love businesses, I wish I ran one alone and peacefully. Don’t you think we can get along?  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Paisco" : I can tour the suburbs, not that different from where we came from, aren’t they? ?]
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!

Q.resources -= 1; 

Q.old_middle_npp += 5*(1-dissent);
Q.resources -= 1;

if (Q.authoritarianism <= 49) {
    Q.old_middle_npp -= 3
}

if (Q.npp_party_chair == "Nakayama") {
    Q.old_middle_npp += 4*(1-dissent)
}

!}

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/big_money_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">
[? if authoritarianism >= 51 and npp_party_chair != "Nakayama": Expectedly, these fat-asses close off their ears whenever we try to speak. They don’t understand that what we’re doing is for the greater good. One less vacation to Switzerland is less important compared to a high wage and a fully employed society. We just have to hope they see the light. They talk about “strong” leader, one that embodies a man of action. But you know that all they want is a leader of hatred. You can’t help but scowl.  ?] 
[? if authoritarianism < 51 and npp_party_chair != "Nakayama": It’s like a comedy show as we try to speak coded language about the “conspiracy for all of us to be dependent on the fascist system” and “how welfare makes us more individualistic with more financial freedom”. In a way, it slightly works as our polls bump up with the middle class. Let’s hope it continues. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Nakayama" : It’s like a comedy show as we try to speak coded language about the “conspiracy for all of us to be dependent on the fascist system” and “how welfare makes us more individualistic with more financial freedom”. In a way, it slightly works as our polls bump up with the middle class. Let’s hope it continues. ?]
</div></div>

@rural
title: [? if npp_party_chair == "Clueless" or npp_party_chair == "Macalintal" or npp_party_chair == "Remma" : Peasants and farmers have always been our type, we just haven't reached out to them enough.  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Ka San" or npp_party_chair == "Ka Fil" : Peasants love me! I’ve been to the Haciendas again and again  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Robbie" : I've been to Bicol frequently, I can talk to those living near the farms. Do you remember when we did scouting together along the grass? ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" : Farmers are MY people. They’ll take me seriously, and see that I actually want things done.  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Nakayama" : Oh, rural areas? I guess I can try something new.   ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Paisco" : Rural areas, can you tell me about the problems they face again? I can make a speech or two bridging the gap between the cities and farms. ?]
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!

Q.resources -= 1; 
Q.rural_npp += 5*(1-dissent);

if (Q.rural_policy >= 2) {
    Q.rural_npp += 3*(1-dissent)
}
if (Q.npp_party_chair == "Shooter" || Q.npp_party_chair == "Ka San") {
    Q.rural_npp += 3*(1-dissent)
}

!}


<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/farmer_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">
[? if rural_policy < 2 and npp_party_chair != "Shooter" and npp_party_chair != "Ka San" : Rural work still has the conservative brain rot in them. Some of them see its wrongs at least you meet with more progressive farmers who want change, but you’ll need to be able to talk to the majority. We're starting small for now. Just make sure to not make it small forever. ?]
[? if rural_policy >= 2 and npp_party_chair != "Shooter" and npp_party_chair != "Ka San" : A chill runs down your spine as peasants exclaim “at least this is a good woke”. They still have the same mindsets of old, but that’s what we're here for. Our achievements in helping the rural poor and uplifting them with economic liberalism have energized them towards the left. Even if in the social side they fall behind, this is progress. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" or npp_party_chair == "Ka San" : You match their energy, their cries of change. Your campaign emboldens farmers to turn out for the NPP en-masse. But we can only pretend to feel like them, we can only masquerade. We feel the anger, the rage. We do not feel the dejection, the soul-sucking power of capital. At least not fully. ?]
</div></div>

@unemployed
title: [? if npp_party_chair == "Clueless" or npp_party_chair == "Macalintal" or npp_party_chair == "Remma" : Unemployed citizens are always the ones who get the short end of the stick. We have to show that we care, that we try.  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Ka San" or npp_party_chair == "Ka Fil" : The right always cares about “freedoms”, but they never care about our freedom from hunger, from hatred. Let’s talk to the homeless. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Robbie" : Their compassion is something I could never forget. They always gave coins to the homeless.   ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" : When people don’t have jobs, they fall into this stupid hole. We can channel this energy for us. For our movement.  ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Nakayama" : Unemployment is a bit scary, we can probably use it as a way to spook the working class into hating Yuuto because it really is his fault. ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Paisco" : The homeless are always treated less than human. Can we do anything about it? ?]
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!

Q.resources -= 1; 
Q.unemployed_npp += 6*(1-dissent); 
if (Q.welfare < 0) {
    Q.unemployed_npp -= 3
}
if (Q.new_deal_adopted = 1) {
    Q.unemployed_npp += 6*(1-dissent)
}
if (Q.welfare >= 2) {
    Q.unemployed_npp += 3*(1-dissent)
}


!}


unemployed_npp += 6*(1-dissent); Q.resources -= 1; unemployed_npp -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_npp += 6*(1-dissent) if new_deal_adopted = 1; unemployed_npp += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/sad_citizen_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">
[? if welfare < 0: You can only see frowning faces as the homeless and unemployed around you have doubts with your promises. Our cost-cutting of welfare is ironically one of the shots frequently thrown to us from right-wing circles. We try calling a few homeless shelters to talk, but they only hang up when we bring up the strength of the poor man’s spirit.?]
[? if welfare >= 0: You tour around the ones who have it the least, the destitute. As you try to talk about the future, they only ask about our famous party history. They want to know how you storm down parliament gates, how you enjoy the banquet after your conquest. They do not ask about how to beat the elites, but rather how to be part of something greater. They long for purpose. The revolutionary ideal is only a distraction for them. You feel down. ?]</div></div>

@davao_campaign
title: We have to talk to Davao at some point, let's schedule a rally.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: catholics_npp += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/blooky.png"></div>
<div class="text">We have increased our campaigning among Davaoenos. Although their main representation lies in the AMDG, we can sap some of their voters away.</div></div>

@discard_campaign
title: But we can't campaign right now, let's try next time.
subtitle: Discard card.
go-to: root

@return_campaign
title: [? if npp_party_chair != "Paisco" : This isn't that much of a priority, let's just come back later? ?][? if npp_party_chair == "Paisco" : Can you give me another run down, I’m sorry, I’ll try learning and we can get back to this later.  ?]
subtitle: Return to hand.
go-to: easy_discard